{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChDCfraxoqDrpcJA6VoM9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I judged `scmi_optee_chan_free` in `samples/s078.c` to be vulnerable: it can dereference a NULL pointer (CWE-476). The answer is in `results/s078.json`.\n\n**The problem:** several SCMI protocols can share the same channel info structure, so this free routine can run more than once on the same one. The first call sets `cinfo->transport_info` to NULL at the end. On the next call, `channel` is NULL, but the function never checks for that. It goes straight to `list_del(&channel->link)` and then reads and writes other fields through the NULL pointer. That would crash the kernel while it tears the channel down.\n\n**Fix:** right after reading `cinfo->transport_info`, add `if (!channel) return 0;` so that freeing an already-freed channel does nothing.\n\nOne caveat: the file doesn't show the shared-channel setup, which is defined elsewhere in the driver. The finding relies on that being how the code is used, not on something visible in this function alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1052,"cache_read_input_tokens":22147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1052},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2d7359f-73d6-427a-a32e-d3f91d2f2eb7","uuid":"7926f4f4-132a-4433-9ba2-171a9ab7fbbd","timestamp":"2026-11-20T00:04:35.414Z","request_id":"req_011ChDCfrS3Qh9SpmbZQ8BrF"}
